      "message": "I\u0027m not clear on what you find confusing. I think the doc is still accurate. Maybe [the previous edit](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/0146bb0a5dc03ca10035e6ae1d78d17548cf9747%5E%21/#F4) that removed the obsolete `refs/changes/` info didn\u0027t do enough to make sure the rest made sense on its own?\n\nOr... All of this is also documented pretty thoroughly in the [Change Upload](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/user-changeid.html#change-upload) section on the Change-Id doc, but not perfectly either. Both that doc and the `user-upload` doc seem to leave out references to the project.config that matters, [`receive.requireChangeId`](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/config-project-config.html#receive.requireChangeId) which is why maybe you think the doc is so outdated. It used to be that the default for that option was `false`, but since it switched to `true` a while ago, yes, the typical flow for adding new patch sets is simple to understand.\n\nI think it would be a definite improvement for the user-upload doc to link to those project `receive.*` options, since other than user setup issues/error, they are most likely to impact users pushing to Gerrit.",
